id: pm-zpoyg9
title: PmClient activation queue serializes unrelated workspaces and extension-free actions
description: "GH-742: replace process-wide SDK activation serialization with request/workspace-scoped safety so independent embedded tenants can execute concurrently."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: concurrency,extensions,"gh:742",multi-tenant,performance,sdk
created_at: "2026-07-26T13:14:50.610Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T19:45:03.826Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T19:43:34.863Z"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#de74a49829faaec73e28ece0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: noExtensions built-in actions bypass global activation serialization; independent workspace/request registries execute concurrently without cross-request leakage; shared legacy global-state activation remains safely serialized or explicitly configured; deterministic concurrency tests prove both non-blocking and isolation; public SDK docs state the concurrency contract
parent: pm-dj98
severity: high
environment: Node embedded multi-workspace hosts
repro_steps: Run a delayed PmClient action for workspace A concurrently with a built-in noExtensions list/get for workspace B; B waits behind the module-global activation queue.
resolution: AsyncLocalStorage request isolation replaces shared embedded runtime state while explicit cwd mutation remains serialized.
expected_result: Extension-free actions and independent workspace activation contexts execute concurrently while genuinely shared unsafe extension state remains isolated.
actual_result: "Independent no-cwd PmClient actions overlap without registry, command-result, or affected-item leakage; explicit cwd calls retain process safety."
affected_version: 2026.7.26
component: SDK runtime activation
customer_impact: Multi-user embedded hosts suffer cross-tenant head-of-line blocking and throughput bounded by one SDK action at a time per process.
